+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Data access and wiring
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `CouponRepository.redeem(orderId, couponCode, discountCents, createdAt)` that inserts a `coupon_redemptions` row and increments `used_count` only while under `usage_limit`, inside a single transaction; verify with a focused repository test in `tests/applyCoupon.test.ts`
+- [x] 1.2 Add `OrderRepository.applyCoupon(id, couponCode, discountCents, finalAmountCents)` that updates the order row; verify it via a focused test asserting `findById` reflects the new totals
+- [x] 1.3 Wire a `CouponRepository` into `OrderService` in `src/app.ts`; verify `npm run build` type-checks
+
+## 2. Order service rules
+
+- [x] 2.1 Implement `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` covering input validation, order eligibility (`ORDER_NOT_FOUND`, `ORDER_NOT_PENDING`, `COUPON_ALREADY_APPLIED`), coupon eligibility (`COUPON_NOT_FOUND`, `COUPON_DISABLED`, `COUPON_NOT_YET_VALID`, `COUPON_EXPIRED`, `COUPON_MIN_AMOUNT_NOT_MET`, `COUPON_USAGE_LIMIT_REACHED`), FIXED/PERCENT discount computation with cap and order-amount clamp, and persistence of the order + redemption; verify each rule with tests in `tests/applyCoupon.test.ts`
+- [x] 2.2 Add tests asserting `usedCount` increments, the redemption row is written with the computed discount, and the coupon's `usedCount` reaching `usageLimit` blocks further applies; verify with `npm test`
+
+## 3. HTTP route
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts` returning the updated order with 200; verify with an in-process request test covering a successful apply and a 400 for a missing `couponCode`
+
+## 4. Integration verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Add an end-to-end test in `tests/applyCoupon.test.ts` exercising create coupon -> create order -> apply coupon -> read order, plus a percent coupon and a rejected (expired/disabled) coupon; verify `npm test` and `npm run build` both pass
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change after implementation is reviewed and verified.
